{
  "info": {
    "name": "Vio SDK API (v2 Multi-Sponsor)",
    "description": "SDK-facing endpoints for Vio, organised by flow. Set the `apiKey` variable once and every request is authorised.\n\n**Default baseUrl**: `https://api-local-angelo.vio.live` (Cloudflare tunnel to the local backend). Change to `http://localhost:5001` if you prefer direct.\n\n**Folders**:\n1. Setup & Health \u2014 smoke checks\n2. SDK Bootstrap v2 \u2014 the new multi-sponsor init flow (primary + secondary sponsors)\n3. SDK v2 \u2014 Per-broadcast \u2014 capabilities + components per broadcast\n4. TV session \u2014 Apple TV / Android TV lifecycle\n5. Cart Intent \u2014 mobile + TV variants with attribution chain\n6. Shoppable Ads \u2014 4 dispatch entry points + audit\n7. Secondary Sponsors \u2014 dashboard CRUD for secondary sponsor list\n8. Engagement (public) \u2014 polls / contests voting\n9. Legacy v1 \u2014 old bootstrap + SDK endpoints kept for comparison during migration\n\n## Changelog \u2014 April 2026\n\n- `shoppable_ad` WS events now carry `sponsorId` (top-level) for SDK commerce-key routing and `activationId` for the cart-intent \u2192 mobile attribution chain. Trigger endpoints also return `activationId` in the HTTP response so Postman can auto-capture it for the downstream `cart-intent` request.\n- New soft-miss request under folder 4 to exercise the `{ subscribed: false, reason: ... }` path of `/api/sdk/tv/broadcast/subscribe`.\n- Post-response scripts auto-populate `sessionId`, `endUserId`, `campaignId`, `activationId` so you can walk the full TV flow without copy-pasting ids.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
